{"type":"message","id":"a1498f92","parentId":"1ef29fd0","timestamp":"2026-10-31T18:52:35.897Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Design three candidates. Features: decisions show fusedWork < originalWork generally, with some cases fusedWork slightly > originalWork (e.g., example 7 fusedWork > originalWork, and example 1,2 small cases where fused ≈ original). Threshold policy 1.02 would reject some borderline cases. Also selective exposure with consumer_tree threshold 2 in the manual program.\n\nCandidate A: simpler threshold exposure with relaxed cleanup threshold 1.5 (moderate).\nCandidate B: decision-tree on producerElements to avoid materialization in small computations: small producerElements → strict threshold 1.02; large → permissive. Actually small computations with tiny producerElements (128, 1024) fused ≈ original — rejecting those avoids trivial overhead. Use tree: if producerElements le 65536 → threshold 1.02 else 1.2? Note aggregate tree is accept-reject, not threshold payload; tree nodes are decisions. A tree like: if producerElements lt 5000 then accept(false)? Actually tree leaves: {\"threshold\":number} accept if fused <= orig*threshold. So leaf thresholds per subtree.\n\nCandidate C: fusion-sequence (no pointwise rewrite) with region policy on cleanup, using launch/materialization weights.\n\nNode budgets: 31 total including one pointwise decomposition node. Keep trees small.\n\nCandidate A (pointwise-fusion-sequence, \"cand-relaxed-cleanup\"):\nexpose: selective, tree {\"threshold\":1.02}, consumer_tree {\"threshold\":2} (same as manual) — vary instead: tree {\"threshold\":1.05}, consumer_tree {\"threshold\":3}? Hmm. Manual uses threshold tree {threshold:1.02}. I'll vary: expose tree uses leaf 1.02 but with a decision on producerElements to be more permissive for big producers; cleanup threshold 1.5.\n\nCandidate B (pointwise-fusion-sequence): expose tree splitting on fusedWork/originalWork indirectly? Aggregate features in tree: originalWork, fusedWork etc. Tree: if originalWork lt 20000000 → threshold 1.02 else threshold 1.5. Cleanup: decision-tree refusing near-zero-gain fusions (guard small ones): if producerElements lt 4096 then threshold 1.02 else threshold 1.02? Cleanup: use threshold 0.999? No, threshold must accept fused <= orig*threshold. Cleanup applies to non-contraction producers; keep cleanup threshold 1.02 like manual, but consumer_tree 4 for aggressive exposure.\n\nCandidate C (fusion-sequence, no pointwise): region cleanup with max_work_growth 1.02, launch_work 256, materialization_work 8; expose selective with tree splitting on producerElements.\n\nWrite JSONs.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The traces show three regimes: (1) large conv producers with big work reductions (fused ~0.3–0.6× original), (2) small/near-noop decisions where fused ≈ original (producerElements 128–4096), and (3) example 7's pathological cases where fusedWork > originalWork (launch-bound / materialization-heavy small consumers). I'll propose three variants targeting these regimes."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_217e15aba31b48d794d82766","name":"submit_policy","arguments":{"policy_json":"{\"format\":\"kiln-transformation-program/1\",\"id\":\"cand-size-split-exposure\",\"kind\":\"pointwise-fusion-sequence\",\"expose\":{\"format\":\"kiln-fusion-policy/1\",\"id\":\"cand-a-expose\",\"kind\":\"selective\",\"tree\":{\"if\":{\"feature\":\"producerElements\",\"op\":\"lt\",\"value\":10000},\"then\":{\"threshold\":1.02},\"else\":{\"threshold\":1.5}},\"consumer_tree\":{\"threshold\":2}},\"cleanup\":{\"format\":\"kiln-fusion-policy/1\",\"id\":\"cand-a-cleanup\",\"kind\":\"threshold\",\"max_work_growth\":1.02}}"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f8ae47860c5a4057a8f0b07c","name":"submit_policy","arguments":{"policy_json":"{\"format\":\"kiln-transformation-program/1\",\"id\":\"cand-worksize-aggressive\",\"kind\":\"pointwise-fusion-sequence\",\"expose\":{\"format\"